# Normalize line endings: LF in the repo and in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default, set at system
# level). Left alone, that rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout, which shows
# up as a whole-repo "modified" diff with no visible difference and pollutes review
# and pipeline diffs. Declaring eol=lf here pins the current LF-everywhere state.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts must stay CRLF — cmd.exe mis-parses LF-terminated .bat/.cmd.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary — never normalize or diff these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
